From ecea420fea2ad3c6ce0db6ea5f14a59fe088c87f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cary Palmer <24235924+professorpalmer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:23:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] cuda: PTQ1_0 decode on consumer Ampere/Ada: SoA q8
 activations, warp-per-row small-K GEMV, GDN gather fusion (+18% TG)

Three changes to the batch-1 PTQ1_0 path, found by tracing a Bonsai 2 27B decode graph
on an RTX 4070 (sm_89) with CUPTI. Same weights, same bits, output byte-identical.

1. Exact integer sums + warp-transposed (SoA) q8_1 activation layout.
   quantize_q8_1<exact_isum> stores the int16 sum of each 32-value block in ds.y (instead of
   the float input sum) and writes the activations grouped by 32 K-blocks with word w of the
   group contiguous. The ternary vec-dot then accumulates raw trits {0,1,2} with dp4a and
   corrects once per block, removing a __vsub4 per 4 weights (no native SIMD byte subtract on
   sm_8x), and a warp-wide load of "word w" in the small-K geometry hits 1 L1 wavefront instead
   of ~36 (lanes were reading block_q8_1 structs 144 B apart). That LSU pressure, not GDDR,
   capped every PTQ1_0 GEMV at ~370 GB/s. Bytes per column are unchanged when K is padded to
   32*128. Only PTQ1_0 opts in (ggml_cuda_q8_1_exact_isum); other types keep the AoS layout.

2. Warp-per-row geometry for small-K PTQ1_0 GEMVs.
   The generic small_k loop strides K-blocks across the whole 128-thread block, so for K=5120
   (40 blocks) only threads 0..39 ever load anything and two of four warps just hold SM slots
   at __syncthreads. Each warp now owns one row and its 32 lanes stride that row's K-blocks;
   shuffle reduction, no shared memory, no barrier. qkv 391 -> 445 GB/s, lm_head 414 -> 460.

3. Recurrent-state gather folded into the GDN kernel.
   build_rs gathers each layer's live state via GET_ROWS into a temp (3 MB for the 27B) that
   only the GDN kernel reads. In-graph the gather is ~8 us/layer and its dirty output sits in L2
   until the FFN weight stream evicts it, making gate/up GEMVs in GDN layers ~15% slower than
   the identical GEMVs in attention layers. When the GET_ROWS output has no other consumer, the
   graph evaluator skips it and the kernel indexes the cache row s_ids[seq] directly.
   Single-sequence only; GGML_CUDA_GDN_GATHER_FUSION=0 disables.

RTX 4070 12 GB, Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-PTQ1_0, llama-bench -fa on TG128, stock clocks:
  prism @ 9a9394a                 50.9 t/s
  + 1 (SoA / exact isum)          55.7
  + 2 (warp-per-row)              58.1
  + 3 (GDN gather fusion)         60.1   (+18%)

test-backend-ops CUDA0 vs CPU: MUL_MAT 1283/1283, MUL_MAT_ID 1019/1019, GATED_DELTA_NET 39/39,
GET_ROWS 119/119. 400 greedy tokens identical with each change on/off.
